'''''Geranium ''×'' oxonianum''''',  the '''Oxford geranium''', is a [[hybrid (biology)#In plants|hybrid]] variety of [[flowering plant]] in the [[family (botany)|family]] [[Geraniaceae]], which is a 1932 cross of garden origin between ''[[Geranium endressii]]'' and ''[[Geranium versicolor]]''.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.brc.ac.uk/plantatlas/plant/geranium-endressii-x-versicolor-g-x-oxonianum | title = Geranium endressii x versicolor (G. x oxonianum) | work = Online Atlas of the British and Irish Flora | access-date = 13 July 2020}}</ref> Growing to {{convert|0.5|m|ft|abbr=on}} tall by {{convert|1 |m|ft|abbr=on}}, it is a highly variable plant with round palmate leaves and often veined flowers in various shades of pink. It can be [[invasive species|invasive]].<ref name = RHSPF>{{cite web | url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/99605/Geranium-x-oxonianum/Details | title = ''Geranium'' × ''oxonianum'' | website = www.rhs.org | publisher = Royal Horticultural Society | access-date = 14 July 2020}}</ref>

Hardy down to {{convert|-20|C|F|abbr=on}} or below, this tough plant is the source of several garden-worthy [[cultivar]]s. The following have been given the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]]:-
*'A.T. Johnson'<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/58284/Geranium-x-oxonianum-A-T-Johnson/Details | title = ''Geranium'' × ''oxonianum'' 'A.T. Johnson' | publisher = RHS | access-date = 14 July 2020}}</ref> 
*'Beholder's Eye'<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/197527/Geranium-x-oxonianum-Beholder-s-Eye/Details | title = ''Geranium'' × ''oxonianum'' 'Beholder's Eye' | publisher = RHS | access-date = 14 July 2020}}</ref> 
*'Wageningen'<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/55128/Geranium-x-oxonianum-Wageningen/Details | title = ''Geranium'' × ''oxonianum'' 'Wageningen' | publisher = RHS | access-date = 14 July 2020}}</ref>

